4. LIMITS AND CONSTRAINTS FOR LOCAL DEVELOPMENT TESTING
-------------------------------------------------------
To qualify as permitted "Limited Local Development Testing" under Section 3(c), 
Your execution and use of the Software must adhere strictly to all of the 
following operational boundaries:
  
  (a) Single-Workstation Execution: The Software must run solely on a single, 
      physical personal computer or workstation owned or leased by a single 
      individual developer. 
  
  (b) No Network Sharing or Hosting: You may not host, run, or expose the 
      Software on a local network, intranet, shared server, cloud server, 
      or internet environment for access by multiple users, teams, or departments.
  
  (c) No Automated CI/CD/Pipeline Use: You may not integrate, embed, or execute 
      the Software in any automated testing, Continuous Integration (CI), 
      Continuous Deployment (CD), or automated validation pipelines belonging 
      to any organization, company, or team, except for personal, non-commercial 
      automation run strictly on Your own local personal computer.
  
  (d) Data Scale Limit: To ensure the Software is used only as a local query 
      compatibility validation helper and not as a substitute for an enterprise 
      or production database, the local catalog database in use must not 
      exceed 100,000 rows per table and 1 GB of total cumulative storage on 
      Your personal workstation.
  
  (e) No Production Use: You are strictly prohibited from using the Software 
      in any production environment, live application, or for any core 
      commercial business operations.

